{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0001868726","cik":"0001868726","slug":"olaplex-holdings-868726","name":"OLAPLEX HOLDINGS, INC.","ticker":"OLPX","exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sector":"Perfumes, Cosmetics & Other Toilet Preparations","sic":"2844","country":"NY","website":"","listed_years":4.4,"first_annual":"2022-03-08","last_filing":"2026-07-17","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001868726&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["OLAPLEX HOLDINGS, INC. files with the SEC under \"Perfumes, Cosmetics & Other Toilet Preparations\", based in NY, and has been publicly reporting for 4 years.","It reported $417.2m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 2.5% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 72.1%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($96.4m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Gross margin of 72.1% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868726/000186872626000036/0001868726-26-000036-index.htm","accession":"0001868726-26-000036"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 69.5% to 72.1% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868726/000186872626000036/0001868726-26-000036-index.htm","accession":"0001868726-26-000036"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $96.4m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868726/000186872626000036/0001868726-26-000036-index.htm","accession":"0001868726-26-000036"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.5% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868726/000186872626000036/0001868726-26-000036-index.htm","accession":"0001868726-26-000036"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue grew only 2.5% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868726/000186872626000036/0001868726-26-000036-index.htm","accession":"0001868726-26-000036"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-5.1% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868726/000186872626000036/0001868726-26-000036-index.htm","accession":"0001868726-26-000036"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $13.6m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1868726/000186872626000036/0001868726-26-000036-index.htm","accession":"0001868726-26-000036"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 64.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.64,"consecutive":2,"current":0.721,"current_display":"72.1%","threshold_display":"64.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -13.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.13,"consecutiv